  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has since secured a $2M budget approval and expanded its team with experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. Strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology are being explored and established. The project is moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming user interface enhancements and a feedback collection period ending in November."
